osure.  - Third, look for opportunities to gradually add to positions if evidence emerges of stabilization or signs of innovation breakthroughs, especially in the services or wearables segments.  - Lastly, periodically reassess the macroeconomic environment and competitor actions to adjust the stance accordingly.  In essence, this approach combines prudence with readiness—accepting Apple’s potential but avoiding overexposure until the risks are more clearly mitigated. Remembering past mistakes, I will emphasize the importance of not overcommitting under uncertain conditions and regularly updating the view based on evolving data.
